Description: Label new native generator and per-unit credential tmpfs roots before use
 Preserve the original clone, slave propagation, nosuid/nodev flags, tmpfs limits,
 generator execution and child wait/error semantics. Only the actual native raw
 SELinux context selects the fixed labels. Other managers keep stock options.
 The sealed native service executor additionally selects only ten fixed unit root
 labels before reopening its new noswap tmpfs, then validates the actual xattr
 against the immutable path mapping. Generic tmpfs directory reads stay denied.
Origin: vendor
Forwarded: not-needed
Last-Update: 2026-11-25

